---
const notes = "About 30 seconds. Name, what you do, one line on why this topic matters to you. Say up front: the demos are written in Rust, but everything in this talk applies to any language with async/await (JavaScript, Python, C#, Go) and to any database. You don't need to read Rust to follow along.";
---

<div class="s title-slide">
  <div class="flex items-center gap-[1em]">
    <img src="/rubbie-icon.png" alt="" class="title-avatar" />
    <div>
      <p class="strong">rubbie kelvin<span class="s-accent">.</span></p>
      <p class="s-muted">software engineer, nigeria.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-auto">
    <p class="s-kicker">sysconf · 2026</p>
    <h1 class="title-main">the autopsy of an asynchronous deadlock<span class="s-accent">.</span></h1>
    <p class="s-big s-muted mt-[0.5em]">how to find a bug that no single tool will show you.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-auto flex justify-between s-small">
    <span>rubbietheone.com</span>
    <span>examples in rust · ideas for every language</span>
  </div>
  <aside class="s-notes" hidden>{notes}</aside>
</div>

<style>
  .title-slide { padding: 4em 5em; }
  .title-avatar { width: 3em; height: 3em; border-radius: 9999px; }
  .title-main { font-size: 3em; font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.1; max-width: 18em; }
</style>
